  body: "# Available resources and unreasonable expectations in hardship\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\
    \nThe captured guidance considers resources that can actually be drawn on and expressly excludes expectations
    such as approaching food banks or charities, obtaining new credit, selling or pawning possessions,
    moving to cheaper housing or asking friends and family.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe source separately
    addresses family and other household resources and specified disregards. Those details are not a demand
    to disclose personal financial data here. Access to hardship must not be inferred to fail merely because
    one of the listed unreasonable steps was not taken; all conditions and current legal applicability
    remain to be reviewed.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 35175, PDF page 44](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6895c9563080e72710b2e2c6/dmg-ch-35.pdf#page=44)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 35: Hardship.\n- [DMG 35176, PDF page 44](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6895c9563080e72710b2e2c6/dmg-ch-35.pdf#page=44)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 35: Hardship.\n- [DMG 35177, PDF page 45](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6895c9563080e72710b2e2c6/dmg-ch-35.pdf#page=45)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 35: Hardship.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation of
    selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol6-ch35`: PDF SHA-256 `e54a2eb89b7e4d4d4ff30802ef129a0ea6c418e6ece7a4e70d142dcb5a7de18b`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `f636b425bb3f5b43a4d10c90c7d93e6a5e1abecd710a1d751b97704b24345753`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/legacy-jsa-hardship-privation
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source’s limits on available resources constrain the enquiry into whether
      privation would occur; they do not themselves establish an award.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch35/0039
      quote: "35153 The DM, when determining if the claimant is entitled to hardship payments, must determine
        if\nhardship will occur if JSA is not paid."
      locator: DMG 35153
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch35/0045
      quote: "35177 It is not considered reasonable to expect claimants to rely upon\n\n\n1. charities,
        such as food banks, (see DMG 35214)\n\n\n2. increase debts by seeking credit or using or extending
        overdraft facilities (see DMG 35196)\n\n\n3. sell or pawn items to obtain cash (see DMG 35213)\n\
        \n\n4. find cheaper housing (see DMG 35216) or\n\n\n5. ask friends and family for help (see DMG
        35217).\n\n\nThese are not considered available resources. While claimants may be prepared to
        request such help\nthere is no requirement to do so and claimants should not be denied access
        to hardship payments if they\ndon’t."
      locator: DMG 35177
